LUNA's embeddings differed by 2-18% between the CPU and GPUs: its frequency embedding took the phase of the Nyquist bin of each patch's FFT, which GPU FFTs leave with rounding noise in its imaginary part, flipping the phase between pi and -pi. That part is now 0, so LUNA embeds on the CPU as before, MPS agrees with the CPU to 4e-6 and CUDA to 2e-3; the rest on CUDA is PyTorch's TF32 convolutions and fused encoder fast path (3e-6 with both off).
